[{:db/id "q-329230/field-1/6a74e1f521b6c4a829a9acbf303e28f2fbb09ff32df1648e1f2b800dcd09bacf" :answer/id #uuid "1a78e03c-16e4-51ea-9f0c-daa8b8eb2f0e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "e^{-2t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186164018 :answer-field/correct "q-329230/field-1/6a74e1f521b6c4a829a9acbf303e28f2fbb09ff32df1648e1f2b800dcd09bacf" :answer-field/choices ["q-329230/field-1/6a74e1f521b6c4a829a9acbf303e28f2fbb09ff32df1648e1f2b800dcd09bacf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-329230/field-2/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "b132061d-afd4-5ef8-8d19-59a0a21b84a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186164017 :answer-field/correct "q-329230/field-2/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-329230/field-2/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-329230"] :question/problem "Consider the following inhomogeneous system of linear differential equations:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t)+{e}^{-2t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe complementary solution to this system is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}],\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nThen, the general solution of the system is\n\n| $x(t)={x}_{c}(t)+$ {{field-1}} $\\cdot \\,\\,$ |  | $0$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the general solution of an inhomogeneous system can be written as \n\n$$\nx(t)={x}_{c}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{c}(t)$ is the complementary solution (solution of the corresponding homogeneous system) and ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution.\n\nThe forcing term\n\n$$\n{e}^{-2t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nof the inhomogeneous system of ODEs is exponential. Therefore, we assume that the particular solution is also exponential, i.e.\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)={e}^{-2t}[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhere $a,b$  are constants that are to be determined. \n\nCalculating the derivative of ${x}_{p}$ with respect to $t$ gives\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}^{′}(t)=-2{e}^{-2t}[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the unknown constants, we substitute ${x}_{p}$ and ${x}_{p}^{′}$ into our system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{e}^{-2t}[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {e}^{-2t}[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}]+{e}^{-2t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ -2[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-2a \\\\ -2b\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-b \\\\ 4a\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-2a \\\\ -2b\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-b+1 \\\\ 4a-2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-b+1=-2a \\\\ 4a-2=-2b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, we get \n\n$$\nb=2a+1.\n$$\n\n \nSubstituting this into the second equation and solving for $b,$ we have\n\n$$\n4a-2=-2(2a+1)\\,⇒\\,a=0.\n$$\n\nSo, \n\n$$\nb=2(0)+1=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the particular solution is\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)={e}^{-2t}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-332591/selection/362a78ff63cca1b390872b8d740139a8d440d84db8a21afe8440a2b4d309b91a" :answer/id #uuid "25553f5d-5d09-5983-816f-1549d8e7eb94" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)[\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332591/selection/0e1501d5d069b6a33e5fa6e65bf8b7a20ca58f1cee187a0b4ca4c5288d90195a" :answer/id #uuid "32748931-7f26-5805-ba01-385bf3d02d6c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)[\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332591/selection/98f64c562ab0076c4396accc98ed2c6ad7a2b47f590d90708077aee1009c51ac" :answer/id #uuid "6d794a89-ec86-5e94-9864-83428697f0be" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{-t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)[\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{2}\\end{aligned}])" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332591/selection/4049222731792196becc45836650a3fe3622f5af63b26fd7dd68f0b75cd4fb0c" :answer/id #uuid "fdbf3752-796c-51dd-acdf-a378b55d0eab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332591/selection/557e18a252614e3998f5ed29942cee75951396ec4308d0139b0693816f6128ce" :answer/id #uuid "70f5e008-0025-5756-892d-967cd63f2a2f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)[\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332591/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1c8ee952-4d2f-5caa-b815-0b9511e133de" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-332591/selection/557e18a252614e3998f5ed29942cee75951396ec4308d0139b0693816f6128ce" :answer-field/choices ["q-332591/selection/362a78ff63cca1b390872b8d740139a8d440d84db8a21afe8440a2b4d309b91a" "q-332591/selection/0e1501d5d069b6a33e5fa6e65bf8b7a20ca58f1cee187a0b4ca4c5288d90195a" "q-332591/selection/98f64c562ab0076c4396accc98ed2c6ad7a2b47f590d90708077aee1009c51ac" "q-332591/selection/4049222731792196becc45836650a3fe3622f5af63b26fd7dd68f0b75cd4fb0c" "q-332591/selection/557e18a252614e3998f5ed29942cee75951396ec4308d0139b0693816f6128ce"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-332591" :question/id #uuid "cdbef393-ee24-56cd-abfd-6178ddb5b54d" :question/math-academy-id "q-332591" :question/problem "Consider the following inhomogeneous system of linear differential equations:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]x(t)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe complementary solution to this system is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nThen, the general solution of the system can be written as $x(t)={x}_{c}(t)+{x}_{p}(t),$ where ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution. Determine the form of the particular solution ${x}_{p}(t).$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the general solution of an inhomogeneous system can be written as \n\n$$\nx(t)={x}_{c}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{c}(t)$ is the complementary solution (solution of the corresponding homogeneous system) and ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution.\n\nThe forcing term\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nof the inhomogeneous system of ODEs is sinusoidal. Therefore, we assume that the particular solution is also sinusoidal, i.e.\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)[\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},{b}_{1},{b}_{2}$ are constants that are to be determined." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-332591/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3eecbfc4-f7eb-5d4c-bea6-8fd21839804c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-332591"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186167157 :question/answer-fields 17592186164333] {:db/id "q-332745/selection/ma-v1/f189307c1ceed7a5fdb05bb3374bf44ed3206ba61b26252aa7c26592ef74ba34/f431be18e407a9cf888273e2c6a1b2c91f4a027f240b0d4faf5cc6770c0bf37f" :answer/id #uuid "f4ed160e-a1b7-5148-bdea-fb8cd7b370ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332745/selection/ma-v1/f189307c1ceed7a5fdb05bb3374bf44ed3206ba61b26252aa7c26592ef74ba34/68375a23d5139edc508301c833aefc3a327d2ac019c4aae2f0a1398a84041068" :answer/id #uuid "51c70fe8-c8bd-5133-8d0f-be853b837c12" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332745/selection/ma-v1/f189307c1ceed7a5fdb05bb3374bf44ed3206ba61b26252aa7c26592ef74ba34/3f4e79c682aafa58cf2256897c94c721463b3413a457de8bd1187b097f89a9cc" :answer/id #uuid "1b17bf9b-153d-5a87-941f-e75cfd4875ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{2t}[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332745/selection/ma-v1/f189307c1ceed7a5fdb05bb3374bf44ed3206ba61b26252aa7c26592ef74ba34/6e2b2846b2aa3a7f1d700d914bf163aaddd44905a3329291ec9a50d1a74f7349" :answer/id #uuid "3cf84b3d-e85b-5540-823d-015f96b29c46" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{-2t}[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332745/selection/ma-v1/f189307c1ceed7a5fdb05bb3374bf44ed3206ba61b26252aa7c26592ef74ba34/e6c3265eaaf6708e5f511c91c305a78b2b24bfa0baf54c7b9445d555122cde68" :answer/id #uuid "bef0e530-b67c-51b9-a1cb-b99994891620" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{t}(t[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}])" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332745/selection/ma-v1/f189307c1ceed7a5fdb05bb3374bf44ed3206ba61b26252aa7c26592ef74ba34" :answer-field/id #uuid "53ef5b5f-2236-52e0-a664-868954ceb36c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-332745/selection/ma-v1/f189307c1ceed7a5fdb05bb3374bf44ed3206ba61b26252aa7c26592ef74ba34/68375a23d5139edc508301c833aefc3a327d2ac019c4aae2f0a1398a84041068" :answer-field/choices ["q-332745/selection/ma-v1/f189307c1ceed7a5fdb05bb3374bf44ed3206ba61b26252aa7c26592ef74ba34/f431be18e407a9cf888273e2c6a1b2c91f4a027f240b0d4faf5cc6770c0bf37f" "q-332745/selection/ma-v1/f189307c1ceed7a5fdb05bb3374bf44ed3206ba61b26252aa7c26592ef74ba34/68375a23d5139edc508301c833aefc3a327d2ac019c4aae2f0a1398a84041068" "q-332745/selection/ma-v1/f189307c1ceed7a5fdb05bb3374bf44ed3206ba61b26252aa7c26592ef74ba34/3f4e79c682aafa58cf2256897c94c721463b3413a457de8bd1187b097f89a9cc" "q-332745/selection/ma-v1/f189307c1ceed7a5fdb05bb3374bf44ed3206ba61b26252aa7c26592ef74ba34/6e2b2846b2aa3a7f1d700d914bf163aaddd44905a3329291ec9a50d1a74f7349" "q-332745/selection/ma-v1/f189307c1ceed7a5fdb05bb3374bf44ed3206ba61b26252aa7c26592ef74ba34/e6c3265eaaf6708e5f511c91c305a78b2b24bfa0baf54c7b9445d555122cde68"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-332745"] :question/problem "Consider the following inhomogeneous system of linear differential equations:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t)+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nA complementary solution to this system is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}],\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nThen, the general solution of the system can be written as \n$x(t)={x}_{c}(t)+{x}_{p}(t),$\nwhere ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution. Determine the form of the particular solution ${x}_{p}(t).$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the general solution of an inhomogeneous system can be written as \n\n$$\nx(t)={x}_{c}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{c}(t)$ is the complementary solution (solution of the corresponding homogeneous system) and ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution.\n\nThe forcing term\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nof the inhomogeneous system of ODEs is constant. Therefore, we assume that the particular solution is also constant, i.e.\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1},{a}_{2}$ are constants that are to be determined." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-332745/selection/ma-v1/f189307c1ceed7a5fdb05bb3374bf44ed3206ba61b26252aa7c26592ef74ba34"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-333613/field-1/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer/id #uuid "344d3479-0809-54ef-8d07-983ec429dd55" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333613/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "6a7bab3a-65fd-5584-8926-c5dd6d14a2f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333613/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "7fba6d00-821b-5994-85b1-3f6005086aaf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-333613/field-1/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer-field/choices ["q-333613/field-1/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" "q-333613/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-333613/field-2/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "1aa14782-b12d-54f8-9c5a-1b1f1326814d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333613/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "1ccd5c93-38fb-522f-8229-17535271e535" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-333613/field-2/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-333613/field-2/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-333613" :question/id #uuid "65cbc273-bb4c-5450-9f41-87df016d4a17" :question/math-academy-id "q-333613" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]x(t)+[\\begin{aligned}3{t}^{2}-3t-4 \\\\ 2{t}^{2}+4t+3\\end{aligned}],\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the missing coefficients in the solution to the initial value problem, shown above.\n\n$x(t)=$ \n{{field-1}} \n$\\,\\cdot \\,[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-2t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\,+$\n{{field-2}}\n$\\,\\cdot \\,[\\begin{aligned}t{e}^{-2t} \\\\ {e}^{-2t}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2{t}^{2}-3t \\\\ {t}^{2}+t+1\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "We are told that the general solution to the system is \n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-2t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}t{e}^{-2t} \\\\ {e}^{-2t}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2{t}^{2}-3t \\\\ {t}^{2}+t+1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nwhere ${c}_{1},{c}_{2}$ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nNext, we find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}.$ Substituting $t=0$ into the general solution, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2(0)} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0\\cdot {e}^{2(0)} \\\\ {e}^{2(0)}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2\\cdot {0}^{2}-3\\cdot 0 \\\\ {0}^{2}+0+1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}+1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}=-3 \\\\ {c}_{2}+1=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, we get ${c}_{1}=-3.$ From the second equation, we have ${c}_{2}=2.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\nx(t)=-3\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-2t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+2\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}t{e}^{-2t} \\\\ {e}^{-2t}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2{t}^{2}-3t \\\\ {t}^{2}+t+1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-333613/field-1" "q-333613/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6d5ab3ac-770b-58c9-b30f-659773ea1a20"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-333613"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-333636/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "41725fac-5b1f-5bfa-9cb5-9fbd996198d5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333636/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "938944d3-9b3b-5706-8fda-854f7d110f0e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-333636/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-333636/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-333636/field-2/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "6c490d86-04cc-5a6b-b439-edac9a65d782" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333636/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "a39aa98d-2b8a-59d1-9afc-5de2c2d2ea09" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-333636/field-2/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer-field/choices ["q-333636/field-2/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-333636" :question/id #uuid "340d62e4-a003-526e-a45a-50c918b881e5" :question/math-academy-id "q-333636" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]x(t)+[\\begin{aligned}7\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ -5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}],\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the missing coefficients in the solution to the initial value problem, shown above.\n\n$x(t)=$ \n{{field-1}} \n$\\,\\cdot \\,[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t){e}^{-t} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t){e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]\\,-$\n{{field-2}}\n$\\,\\cdot \\,[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t){e}^{-t} \\\\ -\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t){e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "We are told that the general solution to the system is \n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t){e}^{-t} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t){e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t){e}^{-t} \\\\ -\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t){e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nwhere ${c}_{1},{c}_{2}$ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nNext, we find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}.$ Substituting $t=0$ into the general solution, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & =[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\cdot 0){e}^{-0} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\cdot 0){e}^{-0}\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\cdot 0){e}^{-0} \\\\ -\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\cdot 0){e}^{-0}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot 0)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot 0) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot 0)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot 0)\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}+3 \\\\ -{c}_{2}+2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}+3=7 \\\\ -{c}_{2}+2=7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, we get ${c}_{1}=4.$ From the second equation, we have ${c}_{2}=-5.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\nx(t)=4\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t){e}^{-t} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t){e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]-5\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t){e}^{-t} \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t){e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-333636/field-1" "q-333636/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6d5ab3ac-770b-58c9-b30f-659773ea1a20"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-333636"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
